=begin
  libeo: the shared library for the e-scripts.

  Loaded once per session with Script.loadlib('libeo'); definitions persist after the
  library script exits. Script.loadlib never loads it twice, so a script that needs a newer
  copy than the session holds runs libeo again. Then it names the version it was built
  against and the library refuses a mismatch loudly:

    Script.loadlib('libeo')
    Script.run('libeo') if Gem::Version.new(::EO::VERSION) < Gem::Version.new('0.5.0')
    EO.require('0.5.0')

  This file only loads the library. The library itself is scripts/eo/, one file per
  concern; each file opens with what it holds, and README.md has the list.

        author: elanthia-online
  contributors: Nisugi
          game: Gemstone
          tags: library, utility, eo
      required: Lich >= 5.22.0
       version: 0.5.0

  Version Control:
  Major_change.feature_addition.bugfix
  v0.5.0 (2026-11-13)
    - EO::Stow, from eloot 2.15.0: the bags an item is tried in by the STOW list (route),
      the overflow bags in number order (overflow_keys), the bags to open before looting
      (bags_for)
    - EO::Loot, from eloot 2.15.0: what in a room is no loot (junk?, with the name, noun
      and disk lists), whether an item is wanted (wanted?, CATEGORIES), a list as one
      whole-word pattern (words), and LOOT on a dead creature (search, in_hand?, bramble?)
    - EO::Skinning, from eloot 2.15.0: which dead to leave (skip?, sometimes?), a
      bounty's creature (for_bounty), edged or blunt (by_tool), getting ready (prepare),
      the SKIN (skin), standing up after (stand_up)
  v0.4.0 (2026-11-13)
    - EO::Town, from eloot 2.15.0: Four Winds Isle and the way off it (fwi?, leave_fwi),
      the shop to walk to and whether to go (shop_elsewhere?, nearest_shop), a shop in a
      bounty's town within the region (in_region), the trash receptacle (trash_can), the
      locksmith pool's worker (pool_worker)
    - EO::Items, from eloot 2.15.0: MARK's unsellable (marked?), throwing an item away
      (toss), phasing a box and bringing it back (phase, unphase), lifting a curse by 315
      or an eonake gauntlet (lift_curse), waiting for the disk (await_disk)
    - EO::Boxes, from eloot 2.15.0: opening a box, looking in, taking coins once and the
      answers to it, and which emptied box is kept (keep?)
  v0.3.0 (2026-11-13)
    - EO::Containers, from eloot 2.15.0: the OPEN, LOOK IN and CLOSE answers, whether
      Lich has a container's contents (listed?), opening one that does not (ensure_open),
      waiting for contents (contents_ready?), reading them fresh (fresh_contents), close
    - EO::Hands, from eloot 2.15.0: the GET and PUT answers, what the hands hold
      (holding?), freeing one (free_hand), taking an item (take), wearing one (wear),
      putting one in a container (store), and the READY list's STORE and READY
      (stow_ready, return_ready, ready_word)
  v0.2.0 (2026-11-13)
    - EO.use: a script lends the library its own helpers (command, result, wait, go,
      say, and any other by name), and EO.command, EO.result, EO.settle, EO.go2 and
      EO.say call the running script's. Code that moves here from a script goes on
      sending, waiting, walking and printing that script's way
  v0.1.0 (2026-11-13)
    - the loader and the version gate: EO.require, EO.version
=end

# The library's files, in the order they load: a file may use what an
# earlier one defines.
parts = %w[version helpers containers hands town items boxes stow loot skinning]

base = File.join(SCRIPT_DIR, 'eo')
verbose = $VERBOSE
begin
  # a second run in a session redefines every constant; that is the point
  $VERBOSE = nil
  parts.each { |part| load File.join(base, "#{part}.rb") }
ensure
  $VERBOSE = verbose
end
